=== QROC ANSWER-IN-HASH CHECK ===
questionHash signature (src/scripts/import-content.ts):
  questionHash(unitId, type, body, options, examYear, sittingLabel)
No answer parameter exists, and the fingerprint SELECT fetches no answer
column (none exists on questions). Therefore any two QROCs sharing a body
in one unit hash identically regardless of expected answer.

Companion finding: the writer itself drops q.answer (Question has no answer
column; expectedAnswerText lives only on clinical_case_parts). QROC
reference answers survive import only if repeated inside explanation text.
Storage of QROC answers needs a product/schema decision — NOT changed here
(task forbids schema changes).

RESOLVED same day: hashing the answer was attempted first, then rejected —
existing rows store no answer, so an answer-bearing hash can never match
them and every re-run would duplicate QROCs. The hash instead includes the
explanation (stored on both sides, stable across runs); authors keep
reference answers inside explanation text. Verified: dry-run now reports
all 10 skipped-duplicate, 0 to create.
